  "summary": "Van Dam and colleagues argue that mindfulness research has grown rapidly but is hampered by semantic ambiguity, weak measurement, heterogeneous interventions, preliminary clinical evidence, undermeasured adverse effects, and overinterpreted neuroimaging. The article offers a prescriptive agenda: define practices precisely, improve measurement and controls, monitor harms, use stronger open-science methods, and communicate findings with less hype.",
